UV scaling: BoxGeometry(w,h,d,1,1,1) has 24 UV vertices; face order: right(+x), left(-x), top(+y), bottom(-y), front(+z), back(-z). UV for each face spans 0..1. Scale per face:
- +x/-x: u along z (depth), v along y → (d/uv, h/uv)
- +y/-y: (w/uv, d/uv)
- +z/-z: (w/uv, h/uv)

Implementation: iterate faces of 4 vertices each (indices 0-3 face0, 4-7 face1, ...).

```js
function boxGeo(w,h,d,uvScale=6){
  const g=new THREE.BoxGeometry(w,h,d);
  const uv=g.attributes.uv;
  const f=[[d/uvScale,h/uvScale],[d/uvScale,h/uvScale],[w/uvScale,d/uvScale],[w/uvScale,d/uvScale],[w/uvScale,h/uvScale],[w/uvScale,h/uvScale]];
  for(let face=0; face<6; face++){
    for(let i=0;i<4;i++){
      const idx=face*4+i;
      uv.setXY(idx, uv.getX(idx)*f[face][0], uv.getY(idx)*f[face][1]);
    }
  }
  uv.needsUpdate=true;
  return g;
}
```
