```js
await page.evaluate(() => { const A=window.__alhambra; A.renderer.render(A.scene, A.camera); return A.renderer.domElement.toDataURL(); });
```
Since the render happens synchronously right before toDataURL in the same JS task, the drawing buffer is still intact → toDataURL works even without preserveDrawingBuffer. Yes, that's the standard trick.

